+### pi.setSessionModelAndThinkingLevel(model, level)
+
+Set the model and thinking level together for the current live `AgentSession`. The operation validates configured auth, clamps the requested thinking level against the target model, and notifies model/thinking observers only after both values are active. It rejects with the same missing-key error as the host model setter.
+
+Unlike `pi.setModel()` and `pi.setThinkingLevel()`, this operation does not write model or thinking entries to session history and does not update saved defaults. The live selection survives extension reload because the `AgentSession` remains active, but it is not reconstructed in a fresh process or replacement session.
+
+```typescript
+const model = ctx.modelRegistry.find("anthropic", "claude-sonnet-4-5");
+if (model) {
+  await pi.setSessionModelAndThinkingLevel(model, "low");
+}
+```
+
+Successful model changes emit `model_select` with `event.source === "session"`. Thinking changes retain the existing `thinking_level_select` event shape.
+
 ### pi.getThinkingLevel() / pi.setThinkingLevel(level)
 
